    "result_text": "All tests pass. `AcceptanceTest` is the only runnable test class (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract, `AuditLogCapture` is a helper), and the full `mvn test` reports **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule for `POST /api/owners`: it's `true` when more than 80 owners were already created for this owner's registration business day, otherwise `false`. The value is stamped at create time and persisted, so it also comes back on `GET /api/owners/{id}` (the path the acceptance test asserts).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **New pipeline function** `FlagOwnerBulkSignup.java` \u2014 counts existing owners sharing the new owner's (business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate` and sets `bulkSignupWarning = count > 80`. Modeled on `CountOwnerNamesakes`; runs before `SaveOwner` so the new owner isn't counted.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `bulkSignup` step between `namesakes` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n3. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a persisted `Boolean bulkSignupWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"bulk_signup_warning\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it; MapStruct maps it by name automatically.\n\n5. **Schemas** \u2014 added a `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres), and appended a trailing `NULL` to the positional owner seed rows in `hsqldb/data.sql` (the only tested DB using positional inserts; h2/postgres use explicit column lists).\n\nOne design note: the flag is computed and stored at creation time rather than recomputed on read \u2014 a GET-time recount would include owners created *after* this one and wouldn't match the \"already been created\" snapshot the spec describes.",
